index 6c349fb..1b13e6d 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,20 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 2.5.0
+
+### Added
+- Content calendar: a month view and a list of what is coming up, with planned posts and the national campaigns side by side. Pick a day to see its posts and campaigns, plan a new post on it, or move the open post to it. Arrow keys, Page Up and Page Down move around the month.
+- Post text and date: a new group in the editor for the words that go with the graphic (with character counts against X, Bluesky, Threads, Instagram and LinkedIn limits and a copy button) and the day and time to post it. Save to calendar keeps the whole post, its text and every image on this device, so it can be changed right up to the day.
+- Planned posts can be opened, copied, marked as posted, moved to another day or time, taken off the calendar or deleted from the calendar, and the plan can be downloaded as an .ics file for any calendar app.
+- Campaign drafts arrive with suggested post text and hashtags and a suggested day (a week before for countdowns, the first day, the last week, the day after). Plan all drafts in my calendar adds a campaign's whole set in one go, without duplicates, and moving a countdown keeps its days to go in step.
+- A reminder and a count on Calendar when posts are due today, plus earlier ones not yet marked as posted; system notifications include them when turned on.
+- Saved designs show their planned date and can be filtered by Planned, Not on the calendar or Posted, and sorted by date to post.
+- Settings: weeks start on Monday or Sunday, and reminders for planned posts on or off.
+- `copy` and `calendar` link parameters.
+
+### Changed
+- Images that came from a link are copied into saved designs where the host allows it, and saved designs open from those local copies first.
+
 ## 2.4.0
 
 ### Added
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index beb639f..7db7964 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -8,10 +8,18 @@ An unofficial, static, browser-based studio for making on-brand CAMRA social gra
 
 ## What it does
 
-Pick one of 23 post types (or Custom), choose a branch, region or sub-brand logo from the built-in library of every CAMRA logo, add a photo or a decorative icon, then download every size you need: Instagram, Facebook, Twitter/X, Bluesky, LinkedIn, the CAMRA Events site and print. Designs can be saved, shared as links and backed up.
+Pick one of 23 post types (or Custom), choose a branch, region or sub-brand logo from the built-in library of every CAMRA logo, add a photo or a decorative icon, write the text that goes with it, then download every size you need: Instagram, Facebook, Twitter/X, Bluesky, LinkedIn, the CAMRA Events site and print. Designs can be saved, planned in a content calendar, shared as links and backed up.
 
 ![Logo picker](docs/screenshots/logos-dark.png)
 
+## Content calendar
+
+Under Post text and date, write the words that go with the graphic (the counter shows which platforms it fits) and pick the day, and optionally the time, to post it. Save to calendar stores the whole post as a saved design with that date: every form setting, the text, and local copies of every image, so the post can be reopened and changed at any point before the day. The text travels in share links as `copy`; the date stays on this device.
+
+The Calendar button opens a month view and a list of what is coming up. Planned posts and campaigns sit side by side; choosing a day shows both, with buttons to open, copy the text of, mark as posted, move or remove each post, and to plan a new one. Campaign drafts can be planned in one go from Campaigns, each on a suggested day, and a countdown recounts its days to go when moved. On the day, a reminder appears under the top bar and Calendar shows a count. The plan can be downloaded as an .ics file for any calendar app; unlike the campaign feeds it is a snapshot, because the plan only exists in this browser.
+
+![Content calendar](docs/screenshots/calendar-dark.png)
+
 ## Campaigns
 
 The studio knows the national and annual campaigns branches post about: Mild Month, Cider and Perry Month, the Good Beer Guide launch, Members' Weekend, Cask Ale Week, Beer Day Britain and more, listed in [docs/CAMPAIGNS.md](docs/CAMPAIGNS.md). Before each one starts (two to six weeks ahead, depending on the campaign) a reminder appears under the top bar so there is time to schedule posts, and another appears while it is on. Each reminder opens the Campaigns panel, where every campaign has ready-made drafts (countdown, launch, last week, thank you) that open in the editor with your branch and default look, the dates and days to go already filled in.
